1
00:04:26,740 --> 00:04:29,240
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: The Sergeant at Arms is directed to make a proclamation.

2
00:04:30,930 --> 00:04:41,230
Alfredo Sotto Corpuz: All persons are commanded to keep silent under pain of penalty while the impeachment court is in session for the trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte.

3
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:51,160
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: The impeachment trial of Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte is hereby called to order. We shall be led in prayer by Senator Judge Juan Miguel Zubiri.

4
00:04:57,090 --> 00:06:14,860
Sen. Juan Miguel “Migz” F. Zubiri: In the name of the Father, and the Son, and the Holy Spirit. Amen. Dear Lord, we come to you today with prayers for your grace and mercy for our country and our people. As we carry on with our pursuit of truth and justice, may you remind us always of the wisdom of the book of Ecclesiastes 3.1-8. There is a time for everything and a season for every activity under the heavens, a time to be born and a time to die. A time to plant and a time to harvest. A time to kill and a time to heal. A time to tear down and a time to build. A time to weep and a time to laugh. A time to scatter stones and a time to gather them. A time to embrace and a time to refrain from embracing. A time to search and a time to give up. A time to keep and a time to throw away. A time to tear and a time to mend. A time to be silent and a time to speak. A time to love and a time to hate. A time for war and a time for peace. Lord, let everyone in this room be your instruments in ushering in a time of peace, togetherness, and healing for our beloved nation. Amen.

5
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,300
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: The Clerk of Court will now call the roll.

6
00:06:20,760 --> 00:07:03,740
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Roll call of members. Senator-Judge Aquino. Senator-Judge Cayetano, Alan. Senator-Judge Cayetano, Pia. Senator-Judge Dela Rosa. Senator-Judge Ejercito, Senator-Judge Estrada, Senator-Judge Go, Senator-Judge Hontiveros, Senator-Judge Lacson, Senator-Judge Lapid, Senator-Judge Legarda, Senator-Judge Marcoleta, Senator-Judge Marcos, Senator-Judge Padilla, Senator-Judge Pangilinan, Senator-Judge Sotto III, Senator-Judge Tulfo Erwin, Senator-Judge Tulfo Raffy, Senator-Judge Villanueva. Senator-Judge Villar Camille, Senator-Judge Villar Mark, Senator-Judge Zubiri, The Presiding Officer Senator-Judge Escudero, The Senate President Senator-Judge Gatchalian.

7
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:16,800
Sen. Sherwin T. Gatchalian: With 14 Senator-Judges present, the Chair declares the presence of a quorum. In accordance with the Rules of Procedure on Impeachment Trials, the Chair now recognizes the duly elected Presiding Officer to preside over the proceedings of the Impeachment Court.

8
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:31,850
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Mr. Senate President. If there are no objections, we shall dispense with the reading of the journal, journal number 37, for October 12 and October 13 of the Senate, sitting as an impeachment court, and shall consider the same as approved.

9
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:38,860
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The Clerk of Court will please call the case before the impeachment court.

10
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:45,040
Atty. Renato N. Bantug Jr.: Case number 004-2026, in the matter of impeachment trial, Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte.

11
00:07:46,370 --> 00:07:58,460
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Before asking for the appearances of the parties, the Presiding Officer would like to make some remarks. In order to update the senator judges, the parties, and the public with respect to what happened in the course of the recess.

12
00:08:01,540 --> 00:10:12,080
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: The chair deems it necessary to place on record certain developments that have transpired since the adjournment of the proceedings on October 13, 2026. In particular, the chair would like to take this opportunity to appraise the parties of the pleadings and submissions received as well as the corresponding orders issued during the recess. This is intended to place relevant documents on the record. and provide proper context for the continuation of today's proceedings. First, reconsideration of the ruling on the application of Rule 18. Following the decision of the prosecution to withdraw Articles 1, 2, and 4 of the Articles of Impeachment, the Chair stated that the subjudicial principle under Rule 18 of the Rules of Procedure on Impeachment Trials shall no longer apply to the withdrawn articles. After Council for Respondent through Attorney Sison registered its objection to the abandonment of Rule 18, Senator Judge Pangilinan, Move for reconsideration or appeal of the chair's ruling and the body. Authorize the presiding officer to rule on the reconsideration or appeal during the recess. In view of the respondents, November 4, 2026 manifestation, on her non-waiver of Rule 18. The court acting on the appeal of Senator Judge Pangilinan issued an order dated November 5, 2026, resolving the subjudice principle under Rule 18 of the Rules of Procedure on Impeachment Trials shall continue to apply with equal force to all articles of impeachment, whether withdrawn or pending adjudication. And reiterating the August 26, 2026 ruling of the court enjoining all covered persons to refrain from issuing public statements or commentaries in violation of section of rule 18 rather. Second, order the prosecution's formal offer of evidence. In compliance with the court's directive, the prosecution filed its formal offer of evidence on October 20, 2026 and the respondent filed their comment on October 30, 2026. The court resolved the formal offer in its November 5, 2026 order, copies of which were furnished to the panel of prosecutors and counsel for respondent, as well as the senator judges. Accordingly, the prosecution is deemed to have rested its evidence-in-chief on Article 2.

13
00:10:13,760 --> 00:12:47,610
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Next, respondent's manifestation regarding its witnesses. The court has also received the respondents' manifestations dated November 4 and 5, 2026. The November 4 manifestation lists 24 witnesses for the November 9 to 13, 2026 hearings and requests subpoenas for them. The November 5 manifestation withdraws Dean Ralph A. Sarmiento as a witness and requests the recall of the subpoena issued for him. On Dean Sarmiento, the November 5 manifestation is noted. The court clarifies that no subpoena has yet been issued to Dean Sarmiento and thus no withdrawal is necessary. On other witnesses, the respondent by counsel filed a manifestation on November 6, 2026 stating that one of its witnesses, Attorney Suzette Balucanagpunay, who was subpoenaed to appear as its first witness, will undergo MRI examination on November 9 and will thus not be able to appear as scheduled. The respondent does request that her presentation be reset to November 10 and to proceed with the succeeding witnesses. The prosecution filed a comment on respondent's manifestation with request for subpoena dosis tecum on November 6, 2026. The court is in receipt. of the Council for Respondents' Latest Manifestation dated November 7, 2026, listing the intended names of witnesses to be presented from November 9 to 13 and the respective purposes for their testimonies. Accordingly, the court, number 1, grants the respondent's request in her manifestation dated November 6 on witness Suzette Punay that she may appear on November 10. Number 2, notes the November 6 comment of the prosecution and the manifestation. 3. Notes the respondents of the November 7, 2026 Manifestation reiterating her request through counsel for the issuance of subpoenas at the Certificandum Induces Tecum to witnesses Attorney Anel S. Antero, Mr. Chadrin Parian, and Bimar M. Barceliano who are scheduled for presentation on November 9-13 for purposes stated in the Manifestation. Subpoenas will accordingly be issued by the Court today. Finally, On the reclassification of access to exhibits, the presiding officer on November 6, 2026 issued an order governing the classification of exhibits attached to the prosecution's formal offer of evidence and corollary manner and extent of access to it. A copy of the order was furnished to the parties and the senator judges accordingly.

14
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:57,060
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: I think that's all by way of update with respect to what happened during the recess. Appearances of the parties?

15
00:12:59,470 --> 00:13:02,030
Rep. Terry L. Ridon: Good morning, Your Honors. The prosecution is ready.

16
00:13:02,550 --> 00:13:04,530
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Good morning, Honorable Ridon.

17
