Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Jimmy?

45
00:15:12,220 --> 00:15:13,280
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Yes, your honor.

46
00:15:13,760 --> 00:15:14,760
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Engineer Jimmy.

47
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:19,130
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Offer, Attorney Lindon?

48
00:15:20,110 --> 00:15:26,330
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Can we ask the tech, your honor, to flash the offer on the screen, your honor?

49
00:15:26,530 --> 00:15:34,830
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, the tech is directed to kindly flash on the screen the formal, the offer rather, of Attorney Lindon.

50
00:15:45,040 --> 00:15:46,380
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: May I proceed, Your Honor?

51
00:15:49,140 --> 00:15:50,300
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: You may proceed, Counsel.

52
00:15:50,520 --> 00:16:12,410
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Thank you, Your Honor. The testimony of Engineer Jaime G. Adalin is offered to prove that he is the City Assessor of Davao City, his duties and responsibilities, and that he has personal knowledge on tax declarations concerning the real property covered by TCT No.

53
00:16:13,380 --> 00:17:15,120
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: 2024-010,146-2024-010775 to prove that the real property covered by the said transfer certificate of title is disclosed by the vice president in her statement of assets, liabilities, and net worth to prove that the prosecution's accusation that the respondent did not disclose. Said transfer certificate of title and the real property in her statement of assets, liabilities, and net worth is malicious and completely false. To identify and authenticate tax declarations and other related documents concerning the transfer certificate of title number 146-12024010775 and to prove other relevant matters.

54
00:17:17,260 --> 00:17:17,980
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Atty. Tolosa?

55
00:17:18,260 --> 00:18:27,750
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: Yes, Your Honor. Just to abbreviate the proceedings, with respect to the offer number one, we're willing to stipulate regarding the position of this witness and that he has personal knowledge regarding the issuance of the tax declaration covered by the TCT mentioned during the offer. With respect to offer number two, that the testimony of this witness would supposedly establish that that TCT was disclosed in the SALN of the Vice President. We object to that for being improper and misleading. There's no way that this witness could prove that that property indicated in the SALN is the same property covered by the subject TCT. The only thing that this witness could testify on is that Possibly, these two properties are in the same barangay. But that will not in any way prove that they are talking about the same property considering the glaring discrepancies between the two, specifically with respect to the acquisition value.

56
00:18:29,340 --> 00:19:05,100
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: declared into those two documents. And for the reason number three, we also vehemently oppose that, especially their characterization that our position that that property covered by the TCT was not disclosed in the SALN was maliciously and completely false. We take the strongest exceptions to these accusations, Your Honor. It cannot be said that it's completely false because again, just a mere Facial examination of those two documents would show that there are obvious discrepancies between the two.

57
00:19:05,950 --> 00:19:07,150
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Can I reply, Your Honor?

58
00:19:07,650 --> 00:19:13,470
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: No need, counsel. Duly noted, subject to cross, you may proceed with your direct examination, Attorney Lindon.

59
00:19:14,190 --> 00:19:15,090
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Thank you, Your Honor.

60
00:19:16,920 --> 00:19:19,400
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Good morning, Engineer Jaime Adalin.

61
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:20,340
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Good morning, sir.

62
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:23,360
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Please state your name for the record, sir.

63
00:19:24,300 --> 00:19:31,120
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Good morning, Your Honors. I am Jaime Gallinero Adalin. resident of Cabantian, Davao City.

64
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:36,000
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: How long have you been a resident of Cabantian, sir? Am I correct, sir?

65
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:37,040
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Yes, sir.

66
00:19:37,220 --> 00:19:40,040
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: How long have you been a resident of Cabantian, Davao City, sir?

67
00:19:40,140 --> 00:19:43,100
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: More or less, nasa 10 years na ako sa Cabantian, sir.

68
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:46,260
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: What is your profession, sir?

69
00:19:46,860 --> 00:19:52,060
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: I am a civil engineer by profession and at the same time a real estate appraiser.

70
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:55,600
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: How long have you been the civil engineer?

71
00:19:56,400 --> 00:20:02,100
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: I passed the board exam sometime in 1984, so more or less 23 years, sir.

72
00:20:02,780 --> 00:20:06,480
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: How about how long have you been a real estate appraiser?

73
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:16,480
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: I passed the licensure examination sometime in 2015, so that would be 9 years.

74
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:19,820
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: What is your present occupation, sir?

75
00:20:20,280 --> 00:20:23,780
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Currently, I am the city assessor of Davao, sir.

76
00:20:24,660 --> 00:20:28,220
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: How long have you been the City Assessor of Davao City?

77
00:20:28,950 --> 00:20:35,890
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: More or less nasa nine years, although in Cotabato City, galing ako doon in the City Assessor's Office also.

78
00:20:36,620 --> 00:20:41,660
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: What are your duties and responsibilities as the City Assessor of Davao City, Sir?

79
00:20:42,480 --> 00:21:15,020
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Among others, number one is to ensure that all those governing real property shall be properly executed. to establish a systematic real property assessment including a systematic identification and accounting system and also to issue certification as to the records of assessment and other relevant information.

80
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:20,580
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Sir, I just ask you to speak more clearly and louder at the microphone.

81
00:21:20,640 --> 00:21:21,340
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Okay, yes sir.

82
00:21:21,400 --> 00:21:32,250
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Thank you sir. Just a follow-up question, sir, regarding your duties and responsibilities. Does it require you to be familiar with the different barangays in Davao City?

83
00:21:32,730 --> 00:21:33,590
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Yes, sir.

84
00:21:38,930 --> 00:21:43,630
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: What records are maintained in the City Assessor's Office of Davao City, sir?

85
00:21:44,430 --> 00:22:04,640
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Number one, as required by the manual issued by the Department of Finance, of course, the tax declaration, tax month, and other Tax mapping control role, quarterly report on real property assessment, notice of assessment, and all others, sir.

86
00:22:04,900 --> 00:22:08,580
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Are there any other documents, sir? Or is that all you can remember, sir?

87
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:18,520
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: That includes assessment role and property record form or the ownership record form.

88
00:22:19,140 --> 00:22:23,320
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Sir, you mentioned tax maps, correct, sir?

89
00:22:23,680 --> 00:22:24,060
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Yes, sir.

90
00:22:24,350 --> 00:22:26,190
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: What are tax maps, sir?

91
00:22:26,760 --> 00:22:46,630
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Tax maps are one of the most important tools in real property assessment. The tax map establishes a permanent link between real property on the ground and the records of the city assessor's office.

92
00:22:47,880 --> 00:22:50,600
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: How are tax maps created, sir?

93
00:22:51,600 --> 00:23:16,180
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: The tax maps are being created to start with the gathering of data that includes approved survey including also cadastral survey and that will form part of the base map and after such it will be segregated and magkakaroon ng mga section maps, index maps, barangay maps.

94
00:23:17,760 --> 00:23:20,740
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Sino po yung gumagawa ng mga tax map na ito sir?

95
00:23:21,280 --> 00:23:32,820
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: In our office, we have a tax mapping operation division that will take charge of the preparation of the maps including gathering of data and information.

96
00:23:34,830 --> 00:23:39,610
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Pag nagawa na po itong tax map, sino po yung nag-a-approve kung alam niyo po?

97
00:23:40,090 --> 00:23:58,600
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Ang approval po, just to abide with the guidelines prescribed by the BLGF, ang city assessor po ang nag-a-approve. It is prepared by the tax mapper and verified by the division head of the tax mapping operation division.

98
00:23:59,670 --> 00:24:03,450
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Thank you, sir. What is the purpose of a tax map, sir?

99
00:24:04,210 --> 00:24:36,800
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: The purpose of tax map is to properly identify the properties on the ground and to discover properties that may have been covered by assessment. And as I was saying a while ago, it will establish a link. Between the real properties on the ground and the records, without the tax map, it would be hard for us to determine ano ba yung mga properties na wala pang assessment.

100
00:24:37,320 --> 00:24:44,720
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Sir, I would just ask you to clarify, what is this link? Why is it important to establish such link?

101
00:24:45,120 --> 00:24:46,600
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Pardon, sir?

102
00:24:46,740 --> 00:24:50,100
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Why is it important to establish this link you mentioned?

103
00:24:52,960 --> 00:25:15,040
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Again, kapag hindi po kasi natin na-establish sa MAPA yung mga real properties na yan, napakahirap po siyang magawa ng assessment for taxation purposes. At yan din po ang MAPA na ginagamit ng Treasurer's Office for the Collection of Real Property Tax.

104
00:25:15,680 --> 00:25:21,240
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Thank you, Sir. Sir, how do you ensure the accuracy of tax maps?

105
00:25:23,160 --> 00:25:53,570
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: To ensure accuracy, recently, may ginagamit na po tayong tool or yung QGIS map wherein maps are being plotted based on technical description. Nung una, manual po yan siya na parang video drawing lang based on the approved survey but in most cases, other LGUs, other assessors are now Going into QGIS mapping. Ginagawa na po namin yan sa Davao City.

106
00:25:53,930 --> 00:25:56,490
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Sorry sir, can you repeat? What is QDS mapping?

107
00:25:56,830 --> 00:25:58,450
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: QGIS mapping, sir.

108
00:25:58,670 --> 00:25:59,850
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Ano pong ibig sabihin nun, sir?

109
00:26:00,130 --> 00:26:19,920
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: It is somewhat a system that you will encode the technical description as described in the title. Then the technical description, the system will plot the exact geographical presentation. or drone to a scale.

110
00:26:21,300 --> 00:26:29,480
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Okay. So, just to clarify, sir, is it this system which helps in generating the tax maps?

111
00:26:30,040 --> 00:26:31,000
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: You're correct, sir.

112
00:26:32,560 --> 00:26:41,480
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: You also mentioned, sir, that the City Assessor's Office of Davao City also maintains tax declarations, sir. You remember that, sir?

113
00:26:41,840 --> 00:26:42,460
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: You're correct, sir.

114
00:26:43,260 --> 00:26:45,080
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: What are tax declarations, sir?

115
00:26:46,250 --> 00:27:14,760
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Tax declaration is issued by the assessor informing the owner of the property, describing also the description kung ano yung property na yan. Also included there are the market value and the assessed value. Again, as a basis for the city treasurer to compute for the basic and SEF tax.

116
00:27:15,420 --> 00:27:20,060
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Sir, anong tax po ba ang may kinalaman sa tax declaration?

117
00:27:23,320 --> 00:27:30,520
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Basically, yung pong real property tax and SEF or special education fund.

118
00:27:31,990 --> 00:27:39,560
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Ito po bang nabanggit yung real property tax? Pareho lang to sa tinatawag nilang amilyar? O may pagkakaiba po ba?

119
00:27:40,060 --> 00:27:43,560
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Tingin ko pare lang po. Parang old term po yung amilyar na yan.

120
00:27:44,590 --> 00:27:47,670
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Sir, paano po binabayaran yung real property taxes?

121
00:27:48,900 --> 00:28:08,370
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Normally, yung aming tax declaration na in-issue, yun po ang dinadala ng taxpayer sa City Treasurer's Office and then naka-automate na po yan. Pag-present po ng tax declaration, i-compute po yung statement of account ng City Treasurer's Office.

122
00:28:10,260 --> 00:28:13,580
Atty. Lindon Miguel C. Bacquel: Sino po ba yung mga kailangan magbayad ng real property tax?

123
00:28:14,570 --> 00:28:18,190
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Normally, ang magbabayad talaga yung property owner.

