1035
03:48:50,340 --> 03:48:50,820
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Correct.

1036
03:48:51,860 --> 03:48:54,360
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: November 12, 2018, saan ka nagbiyahe?

1037
03:48:56,090 --> 03:48:58,590
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Parang wala po akong record ng November 12.

1038
03:48:58,830 --> 03:49:11,110
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Gusto mo pati CCTV footage, kaya ko ibigay sa'yo eh. November 12, 2018, PR356, China. At two days ka lang sa China. At ang dami mong biyahe

1039
03:49:11,110 --> 03:49:20,900
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: eh. Engineer, meron kang Hong Kong, meron kang Thailand, Australia. Hindi kita nilalakit ha, pero magkano bang sweldo mo para ikaw ay palagi nag-abroad? Nakakapag-abroad?

1040
03:49:22,710 --> 03:49:28,470
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Ang sweldo po ng department is nasa 120,000, something like that, sir.

1041
03:49:28,530 --> 03:49:29,410
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: 20,000 a month?

1042
03:49:29,610 --> 03:49:30,430
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: 120,000.

1043
03:49:30,670 --> 03:49:38,640
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: And yet, noong 2023, pumunta ka ng Australia, nagbiyahe ka doon at tumagal ka ng konti. Palagi ka nang bibiyahe.

1044
03:49:38,840 --> 03:49:39,940
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: You're correct, Your Honor.

1045
03:49:40,780 --> 03:49:59,560
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Okay. Siguro baka may nagregalo sa iyo, nag-sponsor, kaya ka nagpagbiyahe abroad. Otherwise, with 20,000 sa pamasahe papuntang Australia, papuntang China, hindi na enough yun, tama ba? And then I've heard na kasama mo po misis mo. I mean, may kasama kang relative na lang, relative.

1046
03:50:00,100 --> 03:50:00,760
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Pardon, sir?

1047
03:50:00,920 --> 03:50:04,850
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: May kasama kang relative pa ata, nung nagbibiyahe ka sa abroad.

1048
03:50:06,030 --> 03:50:07,470
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Again, Your Honor, pakialit.

1049
03:50:07,980 --> 03:50:18,140
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: You've heard me once. I'm not going to repeat myself anymore. Nag-iisip ka habang nagsasalita ako. But anyway, sige, nagmaang-maangan ka na lang. So, inadmit mo na na ikaw ay nagbyahe ng China?

1050
03:50:18,620 --> 03:50:19,520
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Yes, Your Honor.

1051
03:50:19,660 --> 03:50:20,300
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Very good.

1052
03:50:23,830 --> 03:50:52,990
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Now, kanina sabi mo, commercial property, yung pinakita sa slides, prime bistro restaurant. That's commercial, right? Pero why did you say... Meron mga commercial ginagamit na residential. So magtatayo ka ng restaurant and then hindi ka magtatanggap ng mga customer pero yun ang magiging tulugan mo, yun yung tirahan mo. Is that what you meant?

1053
03:50:53,820 --> 03:51:29,000
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: If I can recall it right, Your Honor, yung picture po na pinakita, hindi ko po i-confirm kung yan ba ay yung subject ng property. At yung sinabi ko po na may possibility, Again, hindi po ako sigurado ko yun yung subject ng discussion. But ang sinasabi ko po na may possibility na kahit po commercial building ang design, but pag ginamit po siya as residential, ang aming pong actual use will be residential.

1054
03:51:30,270 --> 03:51:43,260
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Pakiulit. Magpapatayo ka ng commercial building for commercial purposes and yet... Gagawin mo residential dahil doon ka titira at hindi mo gagamitin para sa negosyo? Is that what you're saying?

1055
03:51:43,740 --> 03:51:45,940
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Meron pong pagkakataon ganun, Your Honor.

1056
03:51:46,180 --> 03:51:59,800
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: And who are these stupid people that would do that? Na magpapatayo ka ng commercial establishments and then hindi mo restaurant, that is, and then titirahan mo as residential. You're not making sense. Anyway, let's continue.

1057
03:52:02,260 --> 03:52:10,620
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Doon sa pinag-usapan natin na... Property. Ano ba yung declared? Commercial or residential?

1058
03:52:12,210 --> 03:52:13,270
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Ang land po?

1059
03:52:13,470 --> 03:52:14,470
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Yes, land.

1060
03:52:14,570 --> 03:52:17,610
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: The land is classified now as residential.

1061
03:52:19,200 --> 03:52:20,280
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Classified as residential?

1062
03:52:20,660 --> 03:52:20,740
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Yes.

1063
03:52:21,160 --> 03:52:47,220
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: So kung classified that as residential, bakit nakapagpatayo ng commercial building doon? So for me, hindi magkapareho yung property na yun. Sa inyo, sabi mo, declared as commercial, sa inyo, assessed as commercial. However, dineclare ni Vice President Roduterte sa kanyang SALN as presidential. So hindi magkakatugma. So those are two different animals.

1064
03:52:49,000 --> 03:52:57,740
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Magkaiba po ang land classification for real property taxation versus the land use zoning classification.

1065
03:53:00,500 --> 03:53:28,740
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Meron pagkakataon na magkaiba yung zoning classification. Versus dun sa ginagawang land classification ng city assessor. Because ang base yan po ng land classification for taxation purposes is the predominant use of the land while the zoning classification meron siyang anticipation. Meron siyang sinasabing in this area ang future development niya will be commercial.

1066
03:53:29,160 --> 03:53:33,680
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: Okay. Last na naman and I will address this to the Presiding Officer.

1067
03:53:33,780 --> 03:53:36,580
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: It's okay, Senator Judge Raffy. You can wind up with your question.

1068
03:53:36,700 --> 03:54:16,800
Sen. Raffy T. Tulfo: The best way para magkaalamanan, hindi na magkakalituan, and then para sa mga prosecution also. Tutal, digitalized naman ngayon ang LRA. So pwede man tayong pumunta sa LRA at tatanungin ano-ano mga properties meron under this person. At lalabas at lalabas yun. Kaysa naman nagdilibati pa tayo rito, we're going back and forth. para alamin kung ano yung mga properties na sa kanya at sinasabing hindi naman daw sa kanya at iba yun. Pero if we go to the LRA and have the LRA pull up all the properties under the name of a certain person, under the name of B. Pizarro, under the name of Max Carpio, then it will be a lot easier. Yun lang. Maraming salamat po.

1069
03:54:17,420 --> 03:54:25,600
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Raffy. Senator Judge Aimee, you're recognized, ma'am. You may proceed when you're ready.

1070
03:54:28,270 --> 03:55:23,030
Sen. Imee Marcos: Just a few questions, Presiding Judge. Maraming salamat po. Yes, Engineer po. The prosecution has already pointed out na yung deed of sale covering the subject property reflects a consideration of 6 million. Yun ang nakasulat doon, 6 million. At pinagdidiskitahan na nasa SALN naman ni VP Sara na yung property na yun covered by a deed of sale has an acquisition cost that's declared in the SALN na 10 million. Parang may discrepancy dun sa 6 million sa deed of sale at 10 million na dineklara sa SALN. Is it correct that the consideration stated in the deed of sale does not necessarily reflect, hindi kinakailangan na identical yun dun sa total acquisition cost ng property dahil may iba pang expenses na pwedeng ginastos para mabili yun? Tama ba yun?

1071
03:55:24,060 --> 03:55:47,680
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: I'm not actually... Over here, Your Honor. The requirement that we require from the real property owners is just to provide the date of sale. However, the valuation shall be based on our approved ordinance prescribing the schedule of market values, Your Honor.

1072
03:55:48,140 --> 03:56:31,290
Sen. Imee Marcos: Oo, tinatanong ko lang kasi dahil alam naman natin yung reflection dun sa deed of sale, minsan may kasunduan yung buyer at saka seller, di ba? Na i-absorb yung sinasabi ni presiding officer na capital gains na 6%, yung 1.5 na dock stamp tax, tapos may local transfer taxes, baka tapos nun marami pa, di ba, may legal fees pa kasi magta-title search ka pa kung ano-ano pang mga gastusin. At syempre yung commission ng broker, alam na natin yun, di ba, kung sino mag-aabsorb nun. So ang sinasabi po ninyo yung deed of sale not necessarily na yun talaga yung complete total lahat na pasok na acquisition cost. Maaring mangyari yung dagdag.

1073
03:56:31,470 --> 03:56:35,510
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: That probably will happen Your Honor.

1074
03:56:35,930 --> 03:56:54,390
Sen. Imee Marcos: Okay, so if that's the case, hindi tayo magtataka, halimbawa binayad sa developer, may VAT pa yun, 12% kaagad yun, so talagang maaring mangyari na mas malaki yung acquisition cost stated sa SALN kesa sa deed of sale po.

1075
03:56:54,610 --> 03:56:56,870
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Yes, that's probably what you will happen, Your Honor.

1076
03:56:57,200 --> 03:57:19,460
Sen. Imee Marcos: I see. So final, medyo makulit lang to, no? Pero based on the official assessment records and the identifying particulars dun sa SALN ni VP Sara, can you just tell the impeachment court whether the Matina Crossing property was already included among her declared real properties? Sinabi na ninyo kanina na pwede.

1077
03:57:20,230 --> 03:57:22,570
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Most likely yan po siya, Your Honor.

1078
03:57:22,690 --> 03:57:28,650
Sen. Imee Marcos: Most likely. Pero babalikan ninyo kami at dadalhin yung actual ng mga TCT para masigurado natin

1079
03:57:28,650 --> 03:57:40,470
Sen. Imee Marcos: na totoo nga yun. Yes, Your Honor. Yes, thank you very much, Engineer. At maraming salamat sa presiding judge. Linilinaw ko lang yung presyo na 6 versus 10 million. Salamat po.

1080
03:57:40,730 --> 03:57:41,390
Sen. Imee Marcos: Thank you, Your Honor.

1081
03:57:41,390 --> 03:57:42,530
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you very much, Senator Judge Imee.

1082
03:57:42,770 --> 03:57:43,470
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: Your Honor.

1083
03:57:44,000 --> 03:57:45,020
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Yes, what is your pleasure?

1084
03:57:46,290 --> 03:57:49,770
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: May I be allowed to make a quick manifestation, Your Honor?

1085
03:57:49,890 --> 03:57:51,190
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: In relation to what, counsel?

1086
03:57:51,590 --> 03:58:02,930
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: Acquisition cost, Your Honor, as defined under Memorandum Circular No. 02, Series of 2013, which governs the filing of SALN.

1087
03:58:03,010 --> 03:58:12,110
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Counsel, let the court take care of that. The court can take judicial notice of the law as well as the Memorandum Circular concerning the interpretation of the SALN. And I think it was discussed also before already.

1088
03:58:12,510 --> 03:58:13,150
Atty. Benjamin Tolosa Jr.: We submit yun.

1089
03:58:13,450 --> 03:58:22,260
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Atty. Tolosa. Senator Judge Villanueva is not here yet. So, Senator Judge Erwin is recognized.

1090
03:58:28,280 --> 03:58:38,570
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer. Actually, natanong na po ni Sen. Imee yung gusto ko po itanong sa testigo. May dadaglag lang po ako. Mr. Witness,

1091
03:58:40,630 --> 03:58:49,230
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: I'll just try to check kung medyo kumakakalimutin na kayo. Anyway, papano po kayo napasok sa Davao City Hall, sir?

1092
03:58:50,890 --> 03:58:56,470
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: I transferred sometime in 2002.

1093
03:58:57,990 --> 03:59:01,610
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Okay. From Cotabato City to Davao City, sir. Okay.

1094
03:59:01,750 --> 03:59:05,930
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: So, papano po kayo napuntaroon? Did you apply?

1095
03:59:06,270 --> 03:59:08,430
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Yes, I did apply, Your Honor.

1096
03:59:08,650 --> 03:59:09,630
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Anong posisyon po?

1097
03:59:11,320 --> 03:59:25,660
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: I applied for the position equivalent to my position in the City Assessor of Davao which is Assistant Department Head. And I was appointed as the Assistant City Cooperative Development Officer.

1098
03:59:26,220 --> 03:59:30,500
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Anong kanina pong term ho yun? Sino po yung mayor ng mga panahon po na yun?

1099
03:59:30,680 --> 03:59:35,120
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Ang mayor po at the time ang ating former president na Rodrigo Duterte.

1100
03:59:35,300 --> 03:59:40,440
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Okay. Paano po kayo naging city assessor? Anong year po ito?

1101
03:59:40,800 --> 03:59:42,880
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: That was in 2017.

1102
03:59:45,440 --> 03:59:47,740
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Sino po ang mayor nga po ulit?

1103
03:59:47,980 --> 03:59:53,160
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Si former mayor Sara Duterte, Your Honor.

1104
03:59:53,470 --> 03:59:57,710
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Ano pong pwesto ninyo bago po kayo na i-promote niya as city assessor?

1105
04:00:00,000 --> 04:00:03,280
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: At this time, assistant city cooperative officer ako.

1106
04:00:06,290 --> 04:00:13,830
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: I was also designated as the acting building official sometime 2011 and 2013.

1107
04:00:14,730 --> 04:00:23,490
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: So panahon po ni former mayor, now vice president, Sara Duterte, nung ma-promote po kayo as city assessor?

1108
04:00:23,730 --> 04:00:25,130
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: You're correct, Your Honor.

1109
04:00:25,310 --> 04:00:30,090
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Hanggang sa mga panahon po nito, hanggang ngayong araw, kayo pa rin po as city assessor ng Davao?

1110
04:00:30,400 --> 04:00:31,240
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: You're correct, Your Honor.

1111
04:00:31,340 --> 04:00:34,300
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: No further questions, presiding officer, sir.

1112
04:00:34,480 --> 04:00:40,460
Sen. Francis "Chiz" G. Escudero: Thank you, Senator Judge Erwin. Senator Judge Hontiveros is recognized. You may proceed, ma'am, when you're ready. You have two minutes.

1113
04:00:48,170 --> 04:00:52,520
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Salamat po, Mr. Presiding Officer. Maing hapon, Engineer Adalin.

1114
04:00:52,880 --> 04:00:53,600
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Good afternoon, ma'am.

1115
04:00:53,660 --> 04:01:04,740
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Good afternoon, sir. So, ilang mga tanong po. So, ngayon po, pagkatapos ng lunch break, naaalala niyo na po ba kung kailan kayo pumunta ng China?

1116
04:01:05,900 --> 04:01:08,120
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Yun nga po, as per records, January.

1117
04:01:10,220 --> 04:01:14,830
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Actually, nag-inquire po ako dun sa aming admin. Parang January 25 onwards.

1118
04:01:15,470 --> 04:01:16,490
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Itong taon po?

1119
04:01:16,610 --> 04:01:17,750
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Yes. 2026.

1120
04:01:18,110 --> 04:01:25,290
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Sino-sino po yung mga kasama? Oh, bago yun. Saan-saan po sa China kayo pumunta ngayong January 2026?

1121
04:01:26,130 --> 04:01:32,450
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Hindi ko po ma-memorize pero kasama po namin mga department head and others na gustong sumama.

1122
04:01:32,630 --> 04:01:48,490
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Okay. Pupuntahan ko po yun kung sino-sino yung mga kasama nyo. Pero, posible bang pumunta kayo? Nobyembre pa lang ngayon, pumunta po kayo January. Kahit top 3 places sa China na naalala niyong pinuntahan nyo nitong taon lamang?

1123
04:01:50,510 --> 04:01:52,410
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Hindi ko na po talaga ma-remember.

1124
04:01:52,510 --> 04:01:53,490
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Pumunta ba kayong Beijing?

1125
04:01:56,630 --> 04:01:58,370
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Parang. Parang nakapunta po kami.

1126
04:01:58,470 --> 04:01:58,870
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Parang.

1127
04:01:59,800 --> 04:02:24,140
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Pumunta ba kayong Shanghai? Sir, I'm sorry po. Hindi po talaga nakakatawa. Kasi hindi po naka—hindi po kapani-paniwala na isang inhinyero, isang city assessor, na di umano alam yung mga mapang pinepresenta ng defense at ng prosecution, ay hindi po maalala kung saan sa isang malaking bansa pumunta. So pumunta kayong Beijing, pumunta ba kayong Shanghai?

1128
04:02:26,010 --> 04:02:27,210
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: My apologies, Your Honor.

1129
04:02:33,640 --> 04:02:35,400
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Pumunta ba kayong Fujian?

1130
04:02:36,840 --> 04:02:42,620
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Actually, I'm not keen on traveling. Kaya hindi ko na minememorize yung pinupuntahan.

1131
04:02:42,900 --> 04:03:01,580
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: You're not keen on traveling. Pero nag-travel po kayo. Sabi po ni Sen. Erwin kanina marami po kayong nilakbayang mga bansa. And paano po talaga makadalaw sa ibang bansa at makapunta sa higit sa isang lugar na hindi nyo maalala 10 months later? Binline fold po ba kayo?

1132
04:03:01,640 --> 04:03:02,680
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Hindi naman po.

1133
04:03:03,560 --> 04:03:08,000
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Nabanggit po ninyo may kasama kayong mga department heads. Sino

1134
04:03:08,000 --> 04:03:11,080
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: -sino pong mga kasama nyo sa biyahing ito?

1135
04:03:12,240 --> 04:03:26,970
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: If I can recall, yung aming city engineer, yung city treasurer, ano

1136
04:03:29,750 --> 04:03:30,250
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: po ba yan?

1137
04:03:30,780 --> 04:03:39,800
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: At sino pong nagsama sa inyo, sa city treasurer, sa city engineer dito sa ibang lugar sa China? Sino pong nagdala sa inyo doon?

1138
04:03:41,270 --> 04:03:42,670
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: It is a group travel.

1139
04:03:44,470 --> 04:03:48,290
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Hindi po ako ang nag-organize kung saan.

1140
04:03:48,290 --> 04:03:50,550
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Sino pong nag-organize ng group travel na ito?

1141
04:03:50,750 --> 04:03:53,830
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Hindi ko na rin po ma-recall kung sino talaga nag-organize.

1142
04:03:54,710 --> 04:03:57,950
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Sir, lalo na kung official visit ito.

1143
04:03:59,540 --> 04:04:08,340
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Formal visit. Siguro kayo bilang government worker, maalala nyo sino nag-organize ng trip na ito.

1144
04:04:09,110 --> 04:04:12,370
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: It is actually a personal travel, Your Honor.

1145
04:04:12,570 --> 04:04:20,930
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Hindi ito official visit? Personal travel lang? Magkabarkada ba kayo ng city engineer at city treasurer na sama-sama kayong bumabiyahin?

1146
04:04:21,050 --> 04:04:23,350
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Usually po. Nagsasama-sama po kami.

1147
04:04:23,390 --> 04:04:26,130
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Usually. So bumabalik din ako sa tanong ni Senator Erwin.

1148
04:04:29,650 --> 04:04:40,610
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Sweldo sa gobyerno. You're telling us po na lahat ng mga biyahe niyo sa China at sa Australia, sa iba pang mga bansa, sari-sarili niyong gastos ito?

1149
04:04:41,030 --> 04:04:41,790
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Yes, Your Honor.

1150
04:04:42,210 --> 04:04:59,680
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Okay, that's something for us to check po. Okay, dako po ako dun sa mga discrepancies, hindi na lang po dun sa recollection niyo sa mga biyahe. Dito po sa halaga ng lupa. So, magkano po ulit yung nakalagay na acquisition cost dun sa deed of sale na dala ninyo?

1151
04:05:01,950 --> 04:05:06,190
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Wala po akong dalang deed of sale, Your Honor. Tax declaration lang po.

1152
04:05:06,510 --> 04:05:10,270
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Sa tax deck po na dala nyo, magkano po yung nakalagay na acquisition cost?

1153
04:05:11,930 --> 04:05:15,910
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Hindi po nakalagay ang acquisition cost but the market value as indicated.

1154
04:05:16,010 --> 04:05:18,930
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Magkano ang market value na nakalagay sa tax deck na iyan?

1155
04:05:20,300 --> 04:05:27,000
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Yung pong tax declaration na nakalagay dito is 1,864,680.

1156
04:05:27,260 --> 04:05:33,040
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: 1,864,000 pesos. Market value sa tax debt.

1157
04:05:33,280 --> 04:05:34,100
Engr. Jaime G. Adalin: Yes, Your Honor.

1158
04:05:34,240 --> 04:05:42,920
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Okay po. Meron din pong zonal value na 6.177 million pesos. Tama po ba?

1159
04:05:44,720 --> 04:05:46,100
